  "originalQuery": "Your e-commerce platform runs on a Cloud SQL instance using PostgreSQL. Recently, you noticed a spike in transaction rollback errors during peak traffic hours, leading to degraded application performance. You want to implement a proactive monitoring system to catch such issues early and mitigate the impact. What should you do?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Create a Cloud Monitoring metric based on PostgreSQL logs for \"transaction rollback,\" and set up an alerting policy.<br/>B. Schedule a Cloud Function to query the database every minute for transaction rollback statistics and send notifications.<br/>C. Export database logs to Google Cloud Storage daily, and manually review them for rollback patterns.<br/>D. Configure an email alert in the Cloud SQL settings for any failed queries.",
